**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PlanWindowModelTests`

**How to implement.** The constructor window plans a study's material through a job host its shell carries, and a completed plan's report re-renders the Plan step at once (001 §P `RunPlan`; .spec-md §10.2 per-candidate progress with Cancel, §10.4 completion refresh). It hosts the plan job (step 487) as step 412 hosts the study fit. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201, 412) gains `planRuns : PlanJobHost`, documented in one line, and `KitWindowShell.inert` holds `PlanJobHost.inert`, so every shell built as an update of `inert` keeps its behaviour until the windows compose the real host (step 492). (2) Before `TableAndElementRotationModel`: `PlanSurfaceState = { materialOpt : MaterialVersionId option; criterion : PlanCriterion }`, the Plan step's choices, window state never stored. The model gains `planJob : PlanJobState` and `planSurface : PlanSurfaceState` after `studyFit` (step 412), each documented in one line; `initWith` sets `PlanJobState.idle` and `{ materialOpt = None; criterion = DeterminantPlanCriterion }`. (3) On the model extension holding `studyForwardContext` (step 412), each documented in one line: `member model.planMaterials : OpenedMaterial list`, the chosen study's opened materials whose physics is a crystal (`physics.crystalOpt`, step 460), in study order; `member model.planMaterialOpt : MaterialVersionId option`, `planSurface.materialOpt` when `planMaterials` holds it and otherwise the first of `planMaterials`; and `member model.planReportOpt : PlanReport option`, `planJob.job.committedResults` when its `study` is the chosen study's name and its `material` is `planMaterialOpt`. (4) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line, `StudyPlan of PlanMsg` (the Plan step's run and the job's progress and end), `SetPlanMaterial of MaterialVersionId` (taken when `planMaterials` holds it, else nothing changes) and `SetPlanCriterion of PlanCriterion`; none writes. `StudyPlan msg` is `msg.updateWith (PlanEnvironment.create model.kitShell.planRuns model.kit model.studyForwardContext) model.planJob` (step 487), the model taking the answered state. `RunPlan` is not refused under a read-only kit: it writes no kit file, and a read-only open writes no cache (step 485). No queue, second job or option is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlanWindowModelTests.fs`, `module PlanWindowModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over `initInverse` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:initInverse`) loaded from an in-memory kit holding `PlanRunTests`' items, its uniaxial version and a study QZ opening it with g11 and g33 unknown, as `StudyWindowModelTests` loads its kit (step 410), the shell's `planRuns` a test-local host recording its jobs and its cancel or `PlanJobHost.posting` as `PlanJobTests` drives it: `RunPlan starts one plan through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit plans too`: `StudyPlan (RunPlan { study = QZ; material = <the version>; criterion = DeterminantPlanCriterion })` records one job and leaves `planJob.job.isRunning`; a second `RunPlan` records none; `StudyPlan CancelPlan` records the cancel; over the kit opened read-only a `RunPlan` records one job too. `the Plan step plans the chosen study's opened crystal material, the first by default`: with the study opening a crystal version and a tabulated one (built as step 460's facts build it), `planMaterials` is the crystal one alone and `planMaterialOpt` it; `SetPlanMaterial` of a version the study does not open changes nothing; `SetPlanCriterion TargetTracePlanCriterion` sets the surface's criterion. `a plan's end commits its report, which the Plan step shows for its study and material`: through the posting host, `RunPlan` of QZ's version ends with `planReportOpt` `Some` of a report whose `ranked` holds QZ-Z's two candidates, and choosing another study makes it `None`.

**Acceptance.** After the window plans, `StudyPlan` MUST run one plan at a time through the shell's host for the chosen study's crystal material and criterion, under a read-write or read-only kit, and `planReportOpt` MUST show the committed report of that study and material; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RunPlan starts one plan through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit plans too`, `the Plan step plans the chosen study's opened crystal material, the first by default` and `a plan's end commits its report, which the Plan step shows for its study and material`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
